Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
Create a 12-bit counter with enable and asynchronous load functionality. The counter loads a new value when the load signal is high, counts up when the load signal is low, and resets to 0 when the reset signal is high.

// Signals are defined as below:
// (1) reset: Asynchronously resets the counter to 0. Active high.
// (2) load: Asynchronously loads a new value into the counter. Active high.
// (3) data: The new value to be loaded into the counter.
// (4) ena: Enables the counter to count. Active high.
// (5) q: The current value of the counter.
module top_module(
    input clk,
    input reset,
    input load,
    input [11:0] data,
    input ena,
    output reg [11:0] q);

