description:
Design a 32-bit linear feedback shift register (LFSR) counter that generates a pseudo-random binary sequence. The circuit utilizes a clock signal for synchronous operation and a reset signal to initialize the LFSR to a known state. Upon reset, the LFSR starts from a specified value, and during normal operation, it shifts its bits while applying a feedback operation based on specific taps (bits 31 and 28) to produce the next state. The least significant 4 bits of the LFSR are continually output as Q, providing a 4-bit pseudo-random output based on the state of the LFSR.
module top_module(
  input                clk,
  input                rst_n,
  output reg  [31:0]   Q
);

