description:
Design a 4-bit wide logic operation that selectively outputs a combination of the input bits based on their values. The circuit implements a cascading logic structure where, starting from the most significant bit (MSB), if a bit is set to 1, it blocks the propagation of the previous bits; if it is 0, the corresponding output can reflect its original input value. This results in a modified output where lower significance bits only appear in the output if all higher bits are zero. The module effectively acts as a priority encoder for the binary input, allowing the lower significant bits to pass through only if all more significant bits are low.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] data_i,
    output [3:0] data_o
    );

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] data_i,
    output [3:0] data_o
    );wire mux0;
    wire mux1;
    wire mux2;


    assign mux2 = (data_i[3]==1) ? 1'b0 : 1'b1;
    assign mux1 = (data_i[2]==1) ? 1'b0 : mux2;
    assign mux0 = (data_i[1]==1) ? 1'b0 : mux1;


    assign data_o[3] = data_i[3];
    assign data_o[2] =(mux2 & data_i[2]);
    assign data_o[1] =(mux1 & data_i[1]);
    assign data_o[0] =(mux0 & data_i[0]);endmodule

